  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 3211.01 Fabric Breaks, Cuts and Blowout Repairs",
  "priorExpiration": "2016-01-12",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 3211.01 Fabric Breaks, Cuts and Blowout Repairs.\n\n(a) A vehicle shall be rejected if a tire has:\n\n(1) A fabric break;\n\n(2) A cut, break or weather crack which is:\n\na. In excess of one inch in any direction as measured on the outside of the tire; and\n\nb. Deep enough to reach the body cords;\n\n(3) Temporary repairs made with blowout patches or boots;\n\n(4) Any bumps, bulges or knots related to separation or partial failure of the tire structure; or\n\n(5) Any portion of the ply or cord structure exposed through the tread.\n\nSource. (See Revision Notes at Chapter Heading Saf-C 3200) #8915, eff 6-22-07, EXPIRED: 6-22-15\n\nNew. #10886, INTERIM, eff 7-16-15, EXPIRES: 1-12-16; ss by #11016, eff 1-6-16",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c3200.html"
